markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Evaluating AI Use in the Classroom

#### Before using AI for teacher support or student learning, you will want to evaluate whether or not it will meet the needs of your students. To do so, you can use a checklist like the one below:

<br>

<table style="width:100%; max-width:900px; border-collapse:separate; border-spacing:0; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color:#292F36; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<thead>
<tr>
<th colspan="2" style="background-color:#0093A4; color:#FFFFFF; text-align:left; padding:18px 22px; font-size:24px; font-weight:700; line-height:1.3;">
Evaluating AI Use Checklist
</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width:56px; padding:18px 0 18px 22px; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; vertical-align:top;">
<div style="width:22px; height:22px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:4px;"></div>
</td>
<td style="padding:18px 22px 18px 0; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; font-size:18px; line-height:1.45;">
Does this expand access while keeping the challenge?
</td>
</tr>
<tr style="background-color:#F7F8FA;">
<td style="width:56px; padding:18px 0 18px 22px; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; vertical-align:top;">
<div style="width:22px; height:22px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:4px;"></div>
</td>
<td style="padding:18px 22px 18px 0; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; font-size:18px; line-height:1.45;">
Are students still doing the meaningful thinking?
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width:56px; padding:18px 0 18px 22px; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; vertical-align:top;">
<div style="width:22px; height:22px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:4px;"></div>
</td>
<td style="padding:18px 22px 18px 0; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; font-size:18px; line-height:1.45;">
Does this strengthen student voice and identity?
</td>
</tr>
<tr style="background-color:#F7F8FA;">
<td style="width:56px; padding:18px 0 18px 22px; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; vertical-align:top;">
<div style="width:22px; height:22px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:4px;"></div>
</td>
<td style="padding:18px 22px 18px 0; border-top:1px solid #E8ECF0; font-size:18px; line-height:1.45;">
Will this build independence over time?
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<br>

#### If most answers are yes, the design is likely supporting strong teaching and meaningful learning.

## Evaulation Scenarios

#### Take a look at two of the scenarios we saw earlier in this module. We'll use them as example of how to apply the checklist.

#### 👉 Click on the scenario to see how it does against the checklist.

>#### **💬 Quick Reflection:** Take a moment to evaluate each scenario on your own before clicking to show the answer.

<div style="max-width:900px; margin:20px auto; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color:#292F36;">

<details style="margin-bottom:12px; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;">
Scenario A
</div>
<div style="font-size:14px; color:#555;">
A 7th-grade math student is solving multi-step equations and keeps making the same mistake. They ask AI for “a hint only” and then “one worked example that is similar but not the same.” The student completes the problem, compares their steps to the example, and writes a quick note about the error they fixed.
</div>
</summary>

<div style="padding:18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">

<p><strong>Expand access while keeping the challenge? ✔︎</strong><br>
The hint provides support, but the student still solves the original grade-level problem.</p>

<p><strong>Students still doing meaningful thinking? ✔︎</strong><br>
The student analyzes their mistake, compares steps, and reflects on their correction.</p>

<p><strong>Strengthens voice and identity? ✔︎</strong><br>
The reasoning and final solution remain the student’s own.</p>

<p><strong>Builds independence over time? ✔︎</strong><br>
Scaffolded help plus reflection supports skill growth and future problem-solving.</p>

<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Overall:</strong> This design increases access while preserving rigor, ownership, and long-term growth.</p>

</div>
</details>

<details style="margin-bottom:12px; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;">
Scenario B
</div>
<div style="font-size:14px; color:#555;">
An 8th-grade English student writes a literary analysis essay and asks AI to improve clarity and make the writing more sophisticated. The student reviews the suggestions and accepts most of them. The final essay is stronger and now mirrors work typically produced by a 12th-grade student.
</div>
</summary>

<div style="padding:18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">

<p><strong>Expand access while keeping the challenge? ◑</strong><br>
The product improves, but the cognitive challenge of crafting language may be reduced.</p>

<p><strong>Students still doing meaningful thinking? ✖︎</strong><br>
Accepting broad revisions limits the student’s active revision and stylistic decision-making.</p>

<p><strong>Strengthens voice and identity? ✖︎</strong><br>
Heavy rewriting can shift or dilute authentic student voice.</p>

<p><strong>Builds independence over time? ✖︎</strong><br>
Repeated reliance on AI for stylistic upgrades may slow development of writing skills.</p>

<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Overall:</strong> The essay appears stronger, but the design does not fully support independence, ownership, or deep skill development.</p>

</div>
</details>

</div>

MARKDOWN
